    "text": "-"
  },
  {
    "line": 147,
    "column": 2,
    "type": "BECAUSE",
    "text": "because"
  },
  {
    "line": 147,
    "column": 10,
    "type": "BACKTICK_STRING",
    "text": "`An additional dose of MCV should be administered to HIV-infected children receiving HAART following immune reconstitution. If CD4+ T lymphocyte counts are monitored, an additional dose of MCV should be administered when immune reconstitution has been achieved, e.g. when the CD4+ T lymphocyte count reaches 20–25%. Where CD4+ T lymphocyte monitoring is not available, children should receive an additional dose of MCV 6–12 months after initiation of HAART.`"
  },
  {
    "line": 147,
    "column": 468,
    "type": "DOT",
    "text": "."
  },
